From 68c40c832d675fbda76ad5b48ee365950cb719a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:28:38 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 041/104] scripting: cursor events and the cursor in input

The cursor reaches scripts the way SceneScript documents it:

- cursorEnter/cursorLeave as solid layers come and go under the
  cursor, cursorMove when it moved (to the layers under it and the
  one it was pressed on), cursorDown on a press, cursorUp on a release
  over a layer, then cursorClick on the layer it was pressed on.
  Property and text-layer scripts both get them. CursorEvent has
  worldPosition (scene pixels, y up), localPosition (0..size on the
  layer, y up) and hitBox (null: no puppet hit boxes).
- Which layers: every solid image layer (scene.json `solid`, default
  true; "all mouse cursor events will only work on objects marked as
  Solid") with a cursor handler whose quad, as last drawn (parents,
  rotation, mouse parallax; not the camera zoom), holds the cursor,
  shown or hidden. Hidden ones too: WE's scenes guard their handlers
  on thisLayer.visible, and a trigger that hides itself on cursorEnter
  would otherwise get cursorLeave on the next frame. Not topmost-only:
  the docs don't say, and 2325974975's buttons sit under a solid
  trigger layer. Text and particle layers are not hit-tested yet.
- input.cursorWorldPosition is the cursor in scene pixels (y up), was
  always 0 0 0; input.cursorLeftDown is the left button, was always
  false; input.cursorScreenPosition read a value never written (0 0).

Origin: ours
Why: click and hover interactions did nothing (docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B10: S10, S23)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8XbjUdhpEVfhFbe7bj
